# Accounts and cloud saves (src/platform/cloud.ts, supabase/README.md, docs/CLOUD.md).
#
# Production builds (the web game and the iPhone / iPad app) read the public values from .env.production
# (commented out there while the feature is switched off: supabase/README.md, "Switching it on").
# `npm run dev` does not: the dev server stays fully local unless you copy this file to .env.local and fill it in
# (.env.local is git-ignored). To switch the backend on in ONE browser tab instead, run this in its console and
# reload:  sessionStorage.setItem('bl-dev-cloud', JSON.stringify({ url: '<project URL>', key: '<publishable key>' }))
#
# Project URL and publishable (or legacy anon) key: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys.
# Both are meant to ship in the client; row level security keeps every player to their own rows.
# Never put a secret or service_role key in any .env file of this repo.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
